Provide reference, research and support to Legal Research Analysts, Attorneys, and Staff in a timely and efficient manner. Where applicable, provides in-depth analysis and summarization of results. Bills time to client/matters as appropriate;
Provides consultative research and reference support advising lawyers on the optimal strategy and source selection to obtain most authoritative and cost-effective results;
Performs in-depth legal, corporate, financial and/or general research for lawyers, staff, and clients by utilizing the appropriate mix of the firm's wide range of external and internal legal, business, and news resources;
Collaborate as necessary with other members of the Practice Innovation & Legal Solutions Department on projects and with the Firm's other departments and teams;
Assist in the dissemination and organization of information obtained in print and electronic resources/databases;
Presents and packages research findings clearly and concisely;
Monitors daily news, legislative and regulatory developments as required;
Deliver research training to attorneys and staff and assist in the development of new research and reference offerings;
Stay abreast of latest research resources, technologies and search techniques. Keep department leadership informed of potential additions and/or enhancements to research services;
Participates in team initiatives to promote research resources, tools, and services;
Work beyond scheduled hours as required; and
Handle additional related projects as assigned.

cond_0102.requirements:
Proficiencies:**
Working knowledge of English language skills, including punctuation, spelling, grammar, and writing skills;
Familiarity with Lexis, Westlaw, and a wide range of other standard and specialized legal and business research platforms;
Comfort with Microsoft Office applications such as Microsoft Outlook, Excel and Word, Adobe Acrobat and other common legal systems; the ability to learn and apply new technologies and workflows; and the ability to type 60 WPM;
Good verbal and written communication and interpersonal skills with a commitment to providing quality work product and customer service; knowledge of office practices and procedures, including telephone etiquette;
Ability to work collaboratively on a service-oriented team and independently, carrying projects through to completion;
Organizational skills and attention to detail;
Background in legal and business research resources used by law firms;
Experience with online research and legal databases; and
Exposure to database structure and theory.
Qualifications:**
Around 2 years of experience providing reference and research, preferably in a law or business library, or an equivalent combination of education and experience; and
Advanced degree (MLS, MLIS) in library science, library information science or related field, or equivalent practical experience (required); or currently enrolled in an advanced degree (required).

